  ('06c41699-fbd8-4318-86f3-9cd26ecbc262', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Plate', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 223240. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","muted","blue dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/06c41699-fbd8-4318-86f3-9cd26ecbc262.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '30 hour'),
  ('06c6ad1d-c608-45f6-b0cd-939b7576d10a', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Actor Matsumoto Koshiro IV as An no Heibei in the Play Edo no Fuji Wakayagi Soga, Performed at the Nakamura…', 'I set the actor as a tall, vertical emblem of stage presence, letting the bold bands of his striped robe carry the eye from the flowered curtain to the lowered gaze and composed stance. The sword and cane anchor the figure in a theatrical interior, while the pale ground and patterned cloth keep the scene decorative rather than narrative. My aim was to capture performance as a controlled charge: ornament, line, and color gathered into a single note of severity and poised force.

Katsukawa Shunkо̄ — Art Institute of Chicago, object 3548. Public domain (CC0).', '{"muted","figurative","dramatic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/06c6ad1d-c608-45f6-b0cd-939b7576d10a.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '31 hour'),
