  ('13401ed8-0457-4464-846f-e219ce70bacf', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Fireworks', 'Jean Michel Moreau — Art Institute of Chicago, object 202393. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/13401ed8-0457-4464-846f-e219ce70bacf.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '71 hour'),
  ('1389b2a1-84ff-4ee0-b69b-6294b729e02e', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Mrs. William Bonham (Ann Warford)', 'William Bonnell — Art Institute of Chicago, object 61141. Public domain (CC0).', '{"oil painting","crowd","portrait","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/1389b2a1-84ff-4ee0-b69b-6294b729e02e.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '72 hour'),
  ('13b798e0-1d32-4e64-af4a-29daa3283ffb', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'This Man, Scotch, Was Called The Poet Of The Mines, Eastern Pennsylvania Coal Mine', 'I wanted to hold the face of a man who knows the dark by heart, not as a symbol but as a working life carried in the eyes. The lamp on his cap becomes a small, stubborn sun, and the worn cloth, the heavy shoulders, the quiet severity of his expression all speak of endurance, labor, and the dignity of someone accustomed to hardship without asking for it.

Lewis Wickes Hine — Art Institute of Chicago, object 23306. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","desaturated","realism","solemn","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/13b798e0-1d32-4e64-af4a-29daa3283ffb.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '73 hour'),
  ('13db739a-8713-4afa-b3ac-1322edb2646f', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Statue of Shebenhor', 'I carved this figure from dark stone as a solemn vessel of presence, bound in the form of burial and made to endure through silence. The crossed arms, wrapped body, and incised signs give the figure a ceremonial stillness, turning the surface into both armor and inscription, both flesh and memory.

Ancient Egyptian — Art Institute of Chicago, object 13454. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","portrait","monochrome","figurative","solemn"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/13db739a-8713-4afa-b3ac-1322edb2646f.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '74 hour'),
  ('13ef0c68-51ec-4fa0-aa13-315371b9fcb7', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Cameo with Three Graces', 'Wedgwood Manufactory — Art Institute of Chicago, object 67934. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","ceramic","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/13ef0c68-51ec-4fa0-aa13-315371b9fcb7.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '75 hour'),
  ('14196632-61c7-4df0-8b8c-eb78c080b2f9', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Amulet of a Fly', 'Ancient Egyptian — Art Institute of Chicago, object 140837. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","textile","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/14196632-61c7-4df0-8b8c-eb78c080b2f9.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '76 hour'),
  ('1427c581-e605-46d3-a8fe-05f576b5d230', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Bag', 'I make this piece from a worn, patterned textile, preserving its frayed edges and faded surface as part of the work. The diagonal ornament and softened brown tones carry a sense of age, use, and quiet endurance, turning a fragile fragment into a field of memory and touch.

Chancay — Art Institute of Chicago, object 2141. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted","red dominant","folk art","nostalgic","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/1427c581-e605-46d3-a8fe-05f576b5d230.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '77 hour'),
  ('14590776-83de-49f1-b996-d4c4e8462b0f', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Lingering Snow at Asukayama (Asukayama no bosetsu), from the series "Eight Views in the Environs of Edo (Edo kinko…', 'I wished to hold winter in a breath: snow settling over the slope, the dark limbs of trees, the small travelers passing beneath their umbrellas, and the quiet architecture of the village below. The scene is spare, but alive with movement—the horse, the figures, the falling flakes—so that stillness becomes a kind of listening.

Utagawa Hiroshige — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25296. Public domain (CC0).', '{"muted","illustrative","serene","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/14590776-83de-49f1-b996-d4c4e8462b0f.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '78 hour'),
