  ('1e36dae2-1e80-499a-a375-5e677a2fead0', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Tale of Taishokan', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 145673. Public domain (CC0).', '{"vivid","red dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/1e36dae2-1e80-499a-a375-5e677a2fead0.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '119 hour'),
  ('1e822d9d-e554-4bcc-911d-1ee16c975bf4', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Braid', 'I worked in a lace language—dense black stitches and open white gaps moving in a slow horizontal rhythm, with flowerlike and vine-like forms that feel both decorative and bodily. The piece is built around absence as much as line: the empty spaces carry the pattern, turning ornament into a field of breathing, interwoven shadows.

