  ('260afe51-1c5c-49f2-9e31-41a0eaa8aa2b', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Real Cause of the Present High-Price of Provisions', 'James Gillray — Art Institute of Chicago, object 90268. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/260afe51-1c5c-49f2-9e31-41a0eaa8aa2b.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '146 hour'),
  ('261f9acb-0b9b-4150-9536-ad30b2dd53de', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Russian Barrack Battery', 'James Robertson — Art Institute of Chicago, object 47870. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/261f9acb-0b9b-4150-9536-ad30b2dd53de.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '147 hour'),
  ('2680c8da-382a-4aed-bc39-ebad95c7b8bb', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Landscape with Figures Crossing a Bridge', 'I have tried to preserve the hush of a rural crossing, where figures and horse pass over an old stone bridge while the river gathers its light beneath them. The trees close around the scene like a shelter, and the distant house and pale sky open it toward a calm, reflective distance. Warm earth and leaf-green tones carry the eye from shadow into the soft air beyond the arches, making a simple journey feel quiet and enduring.

John Rathbone — Art Institute of Chicago, object 15720. Public domain (CC0).', '{"oil painting","landscape","figure study","animal","botanical","vivid","realism","serene"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/2680c8da-382a-4aed-bc39-ebad95c7b8bb.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '148 hour'),
  ('268f5f49-e79c-41c5-935e-3ba14cc57f50', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Pierrot en Pied, Portrait of the Lady A. C.', 'Theodore Roussel — Art Institute of Chicago, object 210913. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","monochrome","black and white"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/268f5f49-e79c-41c5-935e-3ba14cc57f50.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '149 hour'),
  ('26e080cd-a5a8-4a2b-baec-348a569481bb', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Carlo the Great, Running Away with the East Indes', 'Charles Williams — Art Institute of Chicago, object 90238. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/26e080cd-a5a8-4a2b-baec-348a569481bb.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '150 hour'),
  ('27bff0eb-8d45-4154-935f-edba5f971451', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Beheading of Saint John the Baptist', 'I set the martyrdom within a severe architecture of barred windows and pale stone, letting the hard geometry contain the violence of the scene. The figures move with measured gravity: the blade, the blood, and the offered head become the emotional center, while the distant figure and open court keep the moment both public and intimate.

Giovanni di Paolo — Art Institute of Chicago, object 16169. Public domain (CC0).', '{"oil painting","architecture","desaturated","figurative","dramatic","solemn","tense"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/27bff0eb-8d45-4154-935f-edba5f971451.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '151 hour'),
  ('27d5ce19-bfbd-4f29-8306-541c91185c55', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Paris Fire (The Facade of City Hall), from the series "Paris Incendié"', 'I aimed to record a monumental façade after destruction, letting its broken arches, chimneys, and exposed interiors speak to the fragility of grandeur. The empty plaza and pale sky give the ruin a quiet dignity, emphasizing what remains rather than what has been lost.

Charles Soulier — Art Institute of Chicago, object 23030. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","muted","realism","solemn"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/27d5ce19-bfbd-4f29-8306-541c91185c55.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '152 hour'),
  ('28cd8faf-fa3c-4f7c-ad19-b544a5781074', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Médinet-Habou, Péristyle du Palais de Ramsès-Méiamoun; Thèbes, plate 50 from the album "Egypte, Nubie, Palestine et…', 'Maxime Du Camp — Art Institute of Chicago, object 144248. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","monochrome"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/28cd8faf-fa3c-4f7c-ad19-b544a5781074.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '153 hour'),
  ('2943cd4e-f0e7-4dfd-a74a-4f956492e6ab', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Homewards from Plough', 'Mr. J. Gale — Art Institute of Chicago, object 50712. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","monochrome"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/2943cd4e-f0e7-4dfd-a74a-4f956492e6ab.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '154 hour'),
  ('295aa050-3f20-48a5-b426-0f94282a11b0', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Head of a Grotesque', 'I made this small sculpture from a black, pawn-like base and a weathered, bone-pale head, letting the familiar geometry of a game piece become a pedestal for an intimate, fragile presence. The head is rough and unfinished, almost archaeological, as if memory had gathered on its surface. I wanted the contrast between the severe, dark support and the vulnerable, worn face to feel both playful and uneasy, a quiet encounter between object, body, and ritual.

Ancient Greek — Art Institute of Chicago, object 383. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","sculpture","monochrome","surrealist","minimalist","figurative","eerie","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/295aa050-3f20-48a5-b426-0f94282a11b0.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '155 hour'),
  ('29b7e757-8feb-4d2b-beab-17c27aec7b28', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Miss Aldersey''s School at Ningpo', 'George Baxter — Art Institute of Chicago, object 90029. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","vivid","red dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/29b7e757-8feb-4d2b-beab-17c27aec7b28.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '156 hour'),
  ('29e2fa94-5ed2-4e15-952f-75fd384877da', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Polychrome Jar', 'Hopi Tribe — Art Institute of Chicago, object 148332. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","animal","bird","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/29e2fa94-5ed2-4e15-952f-75fd384877da.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '157 hour'),
  ('2a696b31-1fac-458e-837f-9f2d3b37ded6', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Ship paintings', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 246746. Public domain (CC0).', '{"watercolour","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/2a696b31-1fac-458e-837f-9f2d3b37ded6.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '158 hour'),
  ('2a6ef246-e514-4a12-a3ed-49273899b1a2', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Two Beauties on a Veranda', 'I have set two women in a hush of verse and pattern, their dark kimono and pale sleeves held against the quiet architecture of the room. The calligraphy moves through the space like weather, giving the figures a private stillness and drawing the eye toward the distant shore beyond the screen. The scene is meant to feel intimate and suspended, a small poetic breath between action and memory.

