  ('76c8b98f-f2c5-42eb-9e64-429562ee1cf4', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Carpet', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 28113. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/76c8b98f-f2c5-42eb-9e64-429562ee1cf4.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '473 hour'),
  ('76ee9acd-3513-4f5a-8a76-788b81efdaf4', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Virgin Mary Cradling the Baby Jesus', 'Charles-François Hutin — Art Institute of Chicago, object 210036. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/76ee9acd-3513-4f5a-8a76-788b81efdaf4.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '474 hour'),
  ('77867d0c-78b1-4954-a7d9-fec3fceaba2a', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Guns for Sale, Nashville', 'I framed the pawnbroker’s storefront as a dense little theatre of urban life, where signs, glass, hanging goods, and passing bodies all press against one another. The mannequin stands like a silent customer, dressed for a life it cannot inhabit, while the shopkeeper’s world spills onto the pavement in trunks, tools, and old promises.

Lewis Wickes Hine — Art Institute of Chicago, object 11348. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","muted","realism","nostalgic","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/77867d0c-78b1-4954-a7d9-fec3fceaba2a.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '475 hour'),
  ('78027ba4-3d54-451f-880a-e6385e8d9114', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Fragment (From a Temple Hanging)', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 236376. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/78027ba4-3d54-451f-880a-e6385e8d9114.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '476 hour'),
  ('783a31dd-fabe-48e1-bcc9-1528c6292add', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Planting Fragrant Fungus at the Tiaozhou''an', 'Chen Guan — Art Institute of Chicago, object 76391. Public domain (CC0).', '{"desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/783a31dd-fabe-48e1-bcc9-1528c6292add.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '477 hour'),
  ('78664909-ce2a-4800-bbdb-8b1883a1a8e9', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Ferdinand III, Emperor of Germany (1637–1657)', 'Two gold coins, each suspended by a small looped mount, present paired medallions of sovereign authority. The obverse carries a crowned profile in profile, while the reverse bears a heraldic composition enclosed by inscriptions and ornamental borders. Their polished surfaces, incised lettering, and carefully modeled relief give the pair a ceremonial dignity and a quiet luminosity.

German — Art Institute of Chicago, object 10411. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","portrait","vivid","figurative","dramatic","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/78664909-ce2a-4800-bbdb-8b1883a1a8e9.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '478 hour'),
  ('78c71f5f-8683-4673-a4cc-d704a0a92010', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Fan', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 93302. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","pastel","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/78c71f5f-8683-4673-a4cc-d704a0a92010.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '479 hour'),
  ('78cc07be-848d-45e4-b26c-74c0dd7fbe26', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'IN EO PATRIÆ SPES', 'Alfred Borrel — Art Institute of Chicago, object 143741. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","landscape","botanical","figure study","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/78cc07be-848d-45e4-b26c-74c0dd7fbe26.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '480 hour'),
  ('78cdb614-8564-4b3f-9052-d8701d1868d5', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Green Tara, Seated in Pose of Royal Ease (Lalitasana), with Lotus Stalks on Right Shoulder and Hands in Gestures of…', null, '{}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/78cdb614-8564-4b3f-9052-d8701d1868d5.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '481 hour'),
  ('795c6025-3d0c-49cc-ab1a-95ba8537ca0d', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Amulet of a Lion-Headed Goddess Holding a Scepter', 'Ancient Egyptian — Art Institute of Chicago, object 140350. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","textile","muted","blue dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/795c6025-3d0c-49cc-ab1a-95ba8537ca0d.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '482 hour'),
  ('79a432a2-038d-44c4-97be-30acca71c540', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Pine and cranes', 'I wanted to hold the quiet dignity of the crane and pine together: two long-necked birds, one lifted in watchful grace, the other bending into the needles, their black, white, and muted gold set against the pale ground. The composition feels spare and ceremonial, balancing stillness with the delicate tension of each curve and feather.

Katsushika Taito II — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25004. Public domain (CC0).', '{"vivid","serene","contemplative","illustrative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/79a432a2-038d-44c4-97be-30acca71c540.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '483 hour'),
  ('7a0eca16-c744-4627-a8cd-74d6584aa2cb', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Panel (Furnishing Fabric)', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 145412. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7a0eca16-c744-4627-a8cd-74d6584aa2cb.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '484 hour'),
  ('7a1214e3-9c49-4dc3-95b9-38bbe49f79a2', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Study of the Crescent Moon in "The Ship"', 'William Holman Hunt — Art Institute of Chicago, object 261599. Public domain (CC0).', '{"watercolour","gouache","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7a1214e3-9c49-4dc3-95b9-38bbe49f79a2.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '485 hour'),
  ('7aba5508-be43-4895-bfa1-fc12c4822fb3', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Madonna and Child', 'I have shaped a tender devotional embrace, where the mother’s veil and heavy drapery gather around the child in a quiet rhythm of folds, weight, and gesture. The worn surfaces and softened features give the figures a sense of age and endurance, as though tenderness has been preserved through time as much as through carving.

Spanish — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25552. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","monochrome","figurative","serene","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7aba5508-be43-4895-bfa1-fc12c4822fb3.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '486 hour'),
  ('7b2594eb-bc5b-4af0-8a1c-a5f0aa8792a5', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Dwarf', 'I made this figure as a small, corpulent presence with a solemn, almost watchful face, simplified into broad planes and softened contours. The worn surface and traces of paint are part of the work’s character, suggesting age, handling, and a quiet dignity rather than polish. Its compact body and folded posture give it a grounded, protective stillness, as if it has been waiting in one place for a long time.

Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25278. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","sculpture","monochrome","figurative","solemn","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7b2594eb-bc5b-4af0-8a1c-a5f0aa8792a5.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '487 hour'),
  ('7b3510a0-6f7a-49dc-bab9-a26b18015a44', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Fragment Displaying Stepped-Fret Motif', 'I made this work as a woven field of stepped forms, where the structure of the textile and the looseness of the fiber both remain visible. Warm ochre, red, olive, and slate shapes move across the surface like fragments of a map or a coded pattern, balancing order with the irregular hand of the process.

Nasca — Art Institute of Chicago, object 2061. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","vivid","abstract","geometric","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7b3510a0-6f7a-49dc-bab9-a26b18015a44.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '488 hour'),
  ('7b63d1df-f07c-4401-a67b-ac9c4f48234a', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Four Stages of Matrimony', 'Richard Newton — Art Institute of Chicago, object 90221. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","vivid","red dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7b63d1df-f07c-4401-a67b-ac9c4f48234a.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '489 hour'),
  ('7bf6034b-a920-42c0-a34c-7e051c3447d7', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Stirrup Spout Vessel Incised with Anthropomorphic Fish', 'I built the vessel around a single gesture: a rounded body, a looped handle, and a narrow spout that rises like a reed. The clay remains warm and earthen, while the pale slip and carved lines gather into a watchful animal face, fierce but contained, as if the vessel were also a creature holding its breath.

Moche — Art Institute of Chicago, object 6251. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","monochrome","figurative","dramatic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7bf6034b-a920-42c0-a34c-7e051c3447d7.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '490 hour'),
  ('7c6d5be1-7cb1-4ca1-948e-e72de9fc5315', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Souvenir De L''Exposition Universelle De 1900', 'Jean Baptiste Daniel Dupuis — Art Institute of Chicago, object 143833. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7c6d5be1-7cb1-4ca1-948e-e72de9fc5315.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '491 hour'),
  ('7c86e3ec-91a3-4b51-9f00-930f6c72b762', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Portrait Medallion: Anne of Austria and her Son, the future King Louis XIV', 'Jean Warin, II — Art Institute of Chicago, object 94134. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","portrait","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7c86e3ec-91a3-4b51-9f00-930f6c72b762.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '492 hour'),
  ('7c8b268b-65b7-4c5f-86ac-2a609a33808d', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Place Saint-Sulpice', 'Set before the severe colonnades, the fountain stands as a quiet counterweight to the architecture: carved stone, shadowed niches, and animal spouts give the monument a tactile, almost human presence. I am interested in the way public stone gathers memory and stillness, turning a civic space into a measured study of weight, light, and endurance.

Hippolyte Bayard — Art Institute of Chicago, object 23797. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","muted","realism","solemn","nostalgic","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/7c8b268b-65b7-4c5f-86ac-2a609a33808d.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '493 hour'),
