  ('a05fdb94-2345-4298-9ba4-7ae053aef1be', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Circle of the Traitors; Dante''s Foot Striking Bocca degli Abbate. Inferno, canto XXXII', 'I have gathered the living and the dead upon a cold, luminous shore, where robed souls stand above a troubled sea and the bodies of the judged lie scattered in the water. Fire gathers at the edge of the world, and the rock itself seems quick with faces, so that nature becomes a witness to the soul’s awakening. The work presses upon the imagination as a vision of judgment, release, and terror, exposing the spirit to a light from which nothing can be hidden.

William Blake — Art Institute of Chicago, object 2330. Public domain (CC0).', '{"muted","figurative","illustrative","solemn","dramatic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/a05fdb94-2345-4298-9ba4-7ae053aef1be.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '632 hour'),
