  ('bfd19422-e8a6-45dd-8562-86b5fc54090f', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Karnak, Temple de Khons; Thèbes, plate 28 from the album "Egypte, Nubie, Palestine et Syrie" (1852)', 'Maxime Du Camp — Art Institute of Chicago, object 144226. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","monochrome"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/bfd19422-e8a6-45dd-8562-86b5fc54090f.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '746 hour'),
  ('bffabcdd-21cb-4a12-b010-7985cdb2c45b', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'View on the Grounds of a Villa near Florence', 'Richard Parkes Bonington — Art Institute of Chicago, object 185775. Public domain (CC0).', '{"oil painting","landscape","architecture","figure study","botanical","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/bffabcdd-21cb-4a12-b010-7985cdb2c45b.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '747 hour'),
  ('c1095724-6474-4294-b73d-af8e4059d99d', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Kanaya, from the series "Fifty-three Stations of the Tokaido (Tokaido gojusan tsugi)"', 'I set the road of the Tōkaidō in dialogue with the vast presence of Mount Fuji, letting travelers pass through a landscape that feels both lived-in and timeless. The broad bands of cloud and water carry the eye across the composition, while the small figures remind me how briefly a human journey crosses such enduring scenery. I wanted the print to hold quiet movement: the road, the clouds, and the mountain all seem to breathe together.

Katsushika Hokusai — Art Institute of Chicago, object 2941. Public domain (CC0).', '{"vivid","illustrative","serene","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/c1095724-6474-4294-b73d-af8e4059d99d.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '748 hour'),
  ('c11f02d3-b26e-4edf-b780-9c2455e5315a', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Actors Sawamura Sojuro III as Soga no Juro, Osagawa Tsuneyo II as Oiso no Tora, Azuma Tozo III as Miura Katagai…', 'I bring the theatre into a quiet bower of wisteria, where musicians, actors, and attendants are arranged by line and pattern rather than illusionistic depth. Flat gold, rose, and olive fields hold the figures in a poised rhythm; black contour, sword, fan, and music stands give the scene its theatrical weight.

Torii Kiyonaga — Art Institute of Chicago, object 3636. Public domain (CC0).', '{"vivid","figurative","illustrative","geometric","serene"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/c11f02d3-b26e-4edf-b780-9c2455e5315a.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '749 hour'),
  ('c140c891-bbc9-4899-a1e2-4f3ee66d733e', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Border', 'A narrow band of white lace unfolds like a quiet procession of flowers and curling stems, its openwork breathing against the darkness. I wanted the piece to feel both ornamental and intimate, a delicate architecture of thread that turns repetition into rhythm and surface into a kind of quiet music.

Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25000. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","monochrome","art nouveau","serene","romantic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/c140c891-bbc9-4899-a1e2-4f3ee66d733e.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '750 hour'),
