  ('c96133e3-4f42-49c0-8826-d19e23086bd5', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', '(He is reading a letter) “A date, could it be from the cute Mme Giraud?? Yes, but it could also come from her husband…', 'I give the moment its quiet comedy: a solitary figure, half absorbed and half exposed, receives the letter as both invitation and trial. The room remains spare, almost all breath and shadow, so that the gesture of reading carries the whole drama. Behind him, the pressed traces of print become a kind of murmuring crowd, while his stance and sudden stillness turn a private glance into a small theatre of coquetry.

