  ('d2e12cef-b4a5-4d0e-82be-567b94e00a37', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Vase', 'Artist unknown — Art Institute of Chicago, object 58067. Public domain (CC0).', '{"ceramic","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/d2e12cef-b4a5-4d0e-82be-567b94e00a37.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '815 hour'),
  ('d3115761-b6fa-4b6c-beae-66df17329e44', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Panel', 'I made this textile as an ornamental field of flowers, letting the blooms and scrolling leaves move through a quiet, rhythmic structure. The warm ground carries the brighter blossoms and greenery, giving the surface a ceremonial richness without losing its soft, garden-like character.

Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 25298. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted","folk art","serene","romantic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/d3115761-b6fa-4b6c-beae-66df17329e44.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '816 hour'),
  ('d34a377c-6a2d-4669-9c96-e2a434986633', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Venus and Mars', 'I wanted to give the moment a charged, almost theatrical stillness: the figure carried through a leafy, earthy setting, caught between resistance and surrender, with the small attendant and urn anchoring the scene in a kind of antique theatricality. The glossy surfaces and jeweled greens and reds make the relief feel both decorative and intimate, as if a dramatic episode has been compressed into a private relic.

