  ('ded83a45-4fce-4edb-9d04-76be31824ed1', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Dying Centaur', 'William Rimmer — Art Institute of Chicago, object 51396. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","monochrome"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/ded83a45-4fce-4edb-9d04-76be31824ed1.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '866 hour'),
  ('df0a7abc-ea44-488f-a7c7-8c4d3c820c9f', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Shimada: The Suruga Bank of the Oi River (Shimada, Oigawa Sungan), from the series "Fifty-three Stations of the…', 'I wanted the print to feel like a great journey breathing through the landscape: the river sweeps across the scene with a force that is both beautiful and dangerous, while the travelers and market figures give human scale to the flood. The composition is crowded, but I tried to keep the movement unified, so that the water, the path, and the people all seem caught in one restless current.

