  ('e37c1c8e-3f2b-4d47-ac10-b020d751f4ea', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Vue Générale Prise a l''Ouest, Le Kaire, plate 1 from the album "Egypte, Nubie, Palestine et Syrie," (1852)', 'Aimé Rochas — Art Institute of Chicago, object 143489. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/e37c1c8e-3f2b-4d47-ac10-b020d751f4ea.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '883 hour'),
  ('e405e48e-7c25-4be3-a90c-90d1b0a2c559', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Fragment', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 95136. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","desaturated"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/e405e48e-7c25-4be3-a90c-90d1b0a2c559.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '884 hour'),
  ('e4425fdc-2de8-472e-b9e4-c3101d897447', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Miniature Box on a Stand (Mingqi)', 'I shaped this small glazed vessel as a quiet architecture of box and plinth, its square lid resting like a roof over a hollow base. The green glaze is allowed to thin, stain, and gather at the edges, so that the surface feels handled by time rather than perfected by it. I wanted the piece to hold a restrained tension between container and structure, domestic and monumental, with its hard geometry softened by age and earth.

