  ('eb887027-b6ac-403a-8bd0-258a332525b5', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'The Crucifixion', 'Carlo Crivelli — Art Institute of Chicago, object 111622. Public domain (CC0).', '{"oil painting","botanical","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eb887027-b6ac-403a-8bd0-258a332525b5.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '924 hour'),
  ('eb938fa0-b02d-4e1c-9478-71dce0e26619', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Flannel Armour; Female Patriotism', 'James Gillray — Art Institute of Chicago, object 90290. Public domain (CC0).', '{"etching","vivid"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eb938fa0-b02d-4e1c-9478-71dce0e26619.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '925 hour'),
  ('eb9ef76d-f469-4645-a019-7c498bc082e3', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'St. George Killing the Dragon', 'I composed this small roundel as a chivalric encounter, with the mounted knight and dragon set against a hill crowned by towers, so that the drama unfolds within a crowded, ornamental landscape. The crowded figures, animals, plants, and architecture press inward like a carved emblem, giving the scene both narrative urgency and ceremonial balance.

Master B with Two Crossed Daggers — Art Institute of Chicago, object 3687. Public domain (CC0).', '{"desaturated","illustrative","figurative","dramatic"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eb9ef76d-f469-4645-a019-7c498bc082e3.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '926 hour'),
  ('eba506a8-d334-4140-b247-f6df6545eec7', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Chair Seat', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 228896. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","vivid","red dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eba506a8-d334-4140-b247-f6df6545eec7.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '927 hour'),
  ('ec2588b7-849f-43da-88c2-155719ce89fb', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Fragment from a Border', 'Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 222946. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted","red dominant"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/ec2588b7-849f-43da-88c2-155719ce89fb.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '928 hour'),
  ('ec6748b8-e8c5-4dd5-a7d5-ac50b773ae54', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Abraham Bloemaert', 'I have rendered the sitter in engraved line, enclosing his likeness within an inscribed oval frame and building the face, ruff, hand, and dark costume through restrained tonal gradation. The aim is a grave dignity, where each incised mark contributes to the measured presence and inward composure of the figure.

Nicolas Jansz. (Claes) Visscher — Art Institute of Chicago, object 52. Public domain (CC0).', '{"desaturated","figurative","realism","solemn","contemplative"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/ec6748b8-e8c5-4dd5-a7d5-ac50b773ae54.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '929 hour'),
