  ('ee668342-7f50-4be2-bb28-8b72ae131dcc', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Caesar Sends a Messenger to Cleopatra from The Story of Caesar and Cleopatra', 'Workshop of Willem van Leefdael — Art Institute of Chicago, object 142548. Public domain (CC0).', '{"textile","muted"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/ee668342-7f50-4be2-bb28-8b72ae131dcc.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '940 hour'),
  ('eeb99825-e25d-4c0e-b13f-0885d6bcdbcd', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Panel', null, '{}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eeb99825-e25d-4c0e-b13f-0885d6bcdbcd.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '941 hour'),
  ('eeed34a5-9702-4920-a1d0-1450f31f01d8', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Double-Sided Printing Block with Mongolian Script', 'I carved the inscription into a dark, worn ground, allowing the pressure of the tool and the friction of use to remain part of the surface. The repeated script becomes a rhythm of relief and shadow, neither decoration nor illustration alone but a field of writing that carries weight, memory, and silence. I wanted the monochrome surface to feel both incised and vocal, as if the words were held in the material rather than merely placed upon it.

Unknown artist — Art Institute of Chicago, object 11695. Public domain (CC0).', '{"sculpture","desaturated","gestural","solemn"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eeed34a5-9702-4920-a1d0-1450f31f01d8.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '942 hour'),
  ('eef845e7-22e7-4601-a8e4-764e4bf1c977', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Breaker Boys in Pennsylvania Coal Mine', 'I framed this group shoulder to shoulder, headlamps bright against worn faces and work-wrinkled clothes, to hold a brief moment of fellowship within the heavier truth of labor. Their smiles are small but unguarded, a loosening of the body after strain, and the faded warmth of the tones keeps the scene intimate, sturdy, and alive with the dignity of the people rather than the machinery of their trade.

Lewis Wickes Hine — Art Institute of Chicago, object 23186. Public domain (CC0).', '{"photography","desaturated","realism","nostalgic","playful"}', '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001/eef845e7-22e7-4601-a8e4-764e4bf1c977.jpg', timestamptz '2026-01-01 00:00:00+00' + interval '943 hour'),
